source synthesized, not recorded: Windows. A notched wheel sends WM_MOUSEWHEEL with a delta of WHEEL_DELTA (120) a notch; a precision touchpad sends WM_MOUSEWHEEL with deltas under 120 while the fingers move, and Windows goes on sending smaller ones after the lift (its inertia), with no message marking either end. winit 0.30 (platform_impl/windows/event_loop.rs WM_MOUSEWHEEL) makes each a LineDelta of delta / 120 with phase moved. Notches 80 ms apart, a fast spin 12 ms apart, then the touchpad: 24-48 units every 8 ms, then inertia every 16 ms decaying by 0.93 until a delta rounds to 0.
